# Sample 18 — Reference point
#
# `reference` plots a point without it becoming a condition: it never
# enters the mandatory/preferred interval calculation, so it can't
# affect status, banding or the selected value. Useful for a number the
# reader should see (a CT rating, a downstream relay's own pickup)
# alongside the real criteria, without implying it's one of them.

diagram "Reference point" {
  below "Emergency load" must 5 kA margin 10%
  above "Minimum fault" must 8 kA margin 10%
  above "Downstream relay pickup" reference 9.5 kA

  selected "Setting" midpoint step 0.05 kA
}
